{% set local_problem %}
<p>Meridianville's climate is beautiful, but it's hard on wood. Hot, humid summers provide perfect conditions for rot to develop. When gutters overflow or leak — common with the area's heavy debris load — water saturates the fascia boards. That moisture, combined with humidity that never lets the wood dry completely, leads to rot.</p>

<p>Many Meridianville homes have fascia damage that owners don't even realize. The paint looks okay from the ground, but probe the wood with a screwdriver and it crumbles. We find this damage regularly when doing gutter estimates — and we always recommend fixing it before installing new gutters.</p>

<p>Installing gutters on rotten fascia is a waste of money. The screws won't hold, the gutters will sag and pull away, and you'll be paying for the same job twice. Fix the foundation first, then install gutters that will last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Wood repair involves removing damaged fascia, soffit, or trim and replacing it with new material. The process includes: assessing the full extent of damage (rot often extends beyond what's visible); removing damaged sections back to solid wood; treating adjacent areas to prevent rot spread; installing new fascia using moisture-resistant materials; and prepping the surface for gutter installation.</p>

<p>We use composite or treated lumber that holds up better in Alabama's climate. The result is a solid foundation for your gutters and protection against future rot.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We see fascia damage on almost every gutter job we do in Meridianville. We know what to look for, how to assess the extent of the problem, and how to fix it properly.</p>

<p>Unlike some contractors who only do gutters, we handle the wood repair in-house. One crew, one job, one company standing behind the work. That's simpler for you and ensures everything is done right.</p>
{% endset %}

